WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:11.940
As more people become health-conscious, whether university sports facilities should be open to the public has become a widely discussed question.
随着越来越多的人注重健康，大学体育设施是否应该向公众开放，已成为一个被广泛讨论的问题。

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:16.760
I am in favor of opening them, provided that they are well managed.
我赞成开放这些设施，前提是管理得当。

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.480
There are two main reasons for my view.
我持这一观点主要有两个理由。

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:32.630
First, many residents, especially elderly people and children, lack convenient places to exercise, while university sports fields and courts are often empty during class hours and vacations.
首先，许多居民，尤其是老人和孩子，缺少方便的锻炼场所，而大学的运动场和球场在上课时间和假期却常常空着。

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:40.020
Opening these facilities puts idle resources to good use and encourages more people to stay active and healthy.
开放这些设施能让闲置资源得到充分利用，并鼓励更多人坚持锻炼、保持健康。

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:49.160
Second, sharing facilities brings students and local residents together and builds a closer relationship between the university and the community.
其次，共享设施能拉近学生与当地居民的距离，使大学与社区的关系更加密切。

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:56.570
Of course, opening the facilities may also cause problems such as overcrowding, noise and security risks.
当然，开放设施也可能带来一些问题，比如过度拥挤、噪音和安全隐患。

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:09.110
To prevent these problems, the university could require visitors to register with their ID cards, set specific opening hours and give students priority when the facilities are in high demand.
为了防止这些问题，学校可以要求来访者凭身份证登记，规定具体的开放时间，并在设施使用需求大时让学生优先使用。

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:17.410
With careful management, opening sports facilities to the public will benefit both the university and the local community.
只要管理细致，向公众开放体育设施将使大学和当地社区都受益。
